CORE
libstdcxx.cpp
--cpp20 --object-bits 12
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ the translation unit converts: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^warning: ignoring
Invariant check failed
--
libstdc++ 13's <format> converts: the `scope __format is ambiguous' error
is fixed (test.desc), and so is the goto-conversion invariant failure that
followed it ("function must not return value", visit_format_arg): a
decltype(auto) function whose return operand calls a function with a
still undeduced return type (its body dropped) no longer takes the
operand's placeholder type, N5008 [dcl.spec.auto.general]/13.  Remaining
drops are tracked by test_libstdcxx.desc (KNOWNBUG).
